        "Body": {
          "ContentType": "html",
          "Content": "<div><span><span>Azure Site Recovery now enables failback from Azure VMs to on-premises Hyper-V, even if replication from on-premises to Azure happened to storage account and the failed-over Azure VM uses managed disks.</span></span><span>&nbsp;</span></div><div><span><br></span></div><div><p><span></span><a href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/site-recovery/hyper-v-azure-tutorial\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span><span>Learn more</span></span></a><span>.</span><span></span><span>&nbsp;</span></p></div>",
          "Markdown": "Azure Site Recovery now enables failback from Azure VMs to on-premises Hyper-V, even if replication from on-premises to Azure happened to storage account and the failed-over Azure VM uses managed disks.\n\nLearn more ."
        },
